Initialise all fields unconditionally in a fixed order, keep the score a double from the start, drop the per-row log, and pre-size the array you fully fill:<br><code>function scoreBatch(rows) {
  const out = new Array(rows.length);
  for (let i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
    const row = rows[i];
    out[i] = {
      id: row.id,
      name: row.name ?? null,
      score: row.weight * 1e9 + row.bonus, // double field from the first instance
      flag: row.flagged === true,
    };
  }
  return out; // log aggregated by the caller, not per row
}</code><br>Key moves: one shared Map (no conditional/late fields), the score field's representation generalises to double once and stays there (no Smi guard to fail), one PACKED array filled in order, and logging moved out of the hot loop so the microtask checkpoint isn't starved.

